Note: a to-do list kept in todo.txt.
Note: try "engc.py run todo.eng add milk", then "engc.py run todo.eng", then "engc.py run todo.eng done 1".

set path to "todo.txt".
set tasks to an empty list.
if the file path exists, set tasks to the lines of the file path.

set command to "list".
if the number of items in the arguments is more than 0, set command to item 1 of the arguments.

if command is "add"
  set task to item 2 of the arguments.
  add task to tasks.
  write tasks joined with a new line to the file path.
  say "Added:" and then task.
otherwise, if command is "done"
  set number to item 2 of the arguments as a number.
  say "Done:" and then item number of tasks.
  remove item number from tasks.
  if the number of items in tasks is 0, delete the file path.
  otherwise write tasks joined with a new line to the file path.
otherwise
  if the number of items in tasks is 0, say "Nothing to do.".
  set n to 0.
  for every task in tasks
    add 1 to n.
    say n and then "." and then task.
  that's all.
that's all.
